               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 21-year-old male patient, admitted on 13/10/2019 with a clinical picture consistent with acute appendicitis. On admission, he presented with right lower quadrant pain, fever, and elevated inflammatory markers. Physical examination revealed localised peritoneal irritation at McBurney's point. Abdominal ultrasound confirmed the diagnosis. Blood tests showed leukocytosis with neutrophilia. The patient was kept nil by mouth, commenced on intravenous fluids and antibiotics, and taken to theatre the same day. A laparoscopic emergency appendectomy was performed without intraoperative complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Wound care was provided, and adequate pain management was ensured throughout the stay. The patient was discharged home on 17/10/2019 in good general condition. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks. Yours sincerely.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
